From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Artem Butusov <art.sormy@gmail.com>
Date: Sat, 31 Oct 2026 03:03:21 -0400
Subject: [PATCH] media: cedrus: Add JPEG encoding on the H616

Baseline 4:2:0 JPEG from NV12, 16x16 to 4096x4096, quality through
V4L2_CID_JPEG_COMPRESSION_QUALITY as libjpeg scales the Annex K tables.
The engine codes the scan with the Annex K Huffman tables and takes the
quantisation tables, a rounding offset and a reciprocal per entry, at
0xe0/0xe4; the headers go out through its put-bits path and the end
marker is written by the CPU. Sizes count in 8-pixel units, as the
vendor's library does on this engine.

The same engine answers MJPG, the format FFmpeg and others ask for. The
H.264 encoder's interrupt handlers move to cedrus_enc.c, shared.
